          "type": "paragraph",
          "title": "Identify the representation",
          "text": "In sign magnitude the first bit is the sign: 0 positive, 1 negative. The other seven bits give the magnitude. Its eight-bit range is −127 to +127, with two zero patterns."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "title": "Two’s complement",
          "text": "Eight-bit weights are −128, 64, 32, 16, 8, 4, 2, 1. The range is −128 to +127. For −13: start 00001101, invert to 11110010, add 1 to obtain 11110011. Sign magnitude −13 is 10001101."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "title": "Add and subtract",
          "text": "Add with carries; keep eight result bits. To subtract B from A, add the two’s complement of B. 12 − 19: 00001100 + 11101101 = 11111001, representing −7."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "title": "Check overflow",
          "text": "100 + 40 gives stored bits 10001100. The true total 140 exceeds +127, so signed overflow occurs. A carry out alone does not establish signed overflow."
        }
      ],
      "questions": [
        {
          "id": "l1",
          "kind": "choice",
          "prompt": "Interpret 10000101 as sign magnitude.",
          "answer": "−5",
          "feedback": "Sign 1 means negative; magnitude 0000101 is 5.",
          "options": [
            "−5",
            "−123",
            "133"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "l2",
          "kind": "choice",
          "prompt": "Interpret 11111011 as two’s complement.",
          "answer": "−5",
          "feedback": "−128 + 64 + 32 + 16 + 8 + 2 + 1 = −5.",
